# API & data fetching

## Boundaries

- Keep transport (HTTP/fetch) separate from UI. Prefer small API client helpers over fetch-in-JSX.
- Server routes / BFF: authenticate from the incoming request; don’t rely on browser-only session helpers when a bearer header is available.
- Return consistent error shapes; map upstream status codes honestly (401/403/404/422/500).

## Clients

- Centralize base URL, headers, and JSON parsing.
- Don’t retry non-idempotent mutations by default; be careful retrying 4xx.
- Cancel or ignore stale responses when the user changes filters/pages quickly (AbortSignal or framework query keys).

## Contracts

- Validate inputs at the edge (DTO / Zod / schema).
- Prefer explicit DTOs over leaking raw DB models to clients.
- Version or evolve fields carefully; avoid silent breaking renames in public APIs.

## Performance & safety

- Paginate list endpoints; never unbounded “get all” for large tables in UI defaults.
- Don’t put secrets in query strings.
- Cache with clear keys; invalidate on writes that affect listed data.
